        "original_id": "ad5a9361-784d-5037-8eca-4f49113129e1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alamgir, Ali Azmat, Meesha Shafi, Strings, Shahzad Hasan\n- Projects: Music Icons, Aaina, Aaina soundtrack, Yaaro Yehi Dosti Hai\n- Organizations: ARY Digital\n- Topics: Pakistani pop music, television talent shows\n\nFacts:\n- In 1976, Alamgir produced the album Aaina from the soundtrack of the Urdu-language Pakistani film Aaina.\n- In the early 1990s, Ali Azmat sang the hit song \"Yaaro Yehi Dosti Hai,\" which topped the charts and remained famous.\n- Ali Azmat was born on April 20, 1970, and he is a Pakistani singer-songwriter, musician, and actor.\n- In April 2013, Alamgir joined Meesha Shafi, Strings, Ali Azmat, and Shahzad Hasan as a judge on the singing talent show Music Icons.\n- Music Icons aired on the ARY Digital television channel.",
